+By default, the network broker permits only HTTPS and rejects private, loopback,
+link-local, and metadata-service addresses. A Wealthfolio host can explicitly
+enable a local read-only API by setting `WF_ADDON_NETWORK_PRIVATE_TARGETS` to a
+comma-separated list of exact URLs in the form
+`http://host:port/patrimonio/v4`. For example:
+
+```text
+WF_ADDON_NETWORK_PRIVATE_TARGETS=http://host.docker.internal:5201/patrimonio/v4,http://host.docker.internal:5301/patrimonio/v4
+```
+
+Each configured target permits only `GET` requests to that exact HTTP origin
+and the `/patrimonio/v4` path or its descendants. The addon's
+`network.allowedHosts` must repeat the host literally; wildcards do not qualify
+for local targets. Wildcards, other ports, schemes, paths, link-local/metadata
+addresses, and public DNS results do not qualify in the operator target.
+Redirects and proxy use remain disabled for these requests, and the broker pins
+the resolved addresses. Leave this setting unset unless the Wealthfolio operator
+intends to allow that local API access.
+
